# Shelfmark environment template.
#
# Copy this to `.env` at the repository root for local use (it is git-ignored).
# Never commit a real secret.
#
# The compose API service loads this file directly, so editing `.env` and
# restarting is all it takes:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit .env, then:
#   docker compose -f infra/compose.yaml up --build
#
# The values below also work as shell exports when you run the API or storefront
# as host processes. The API container sets its own data-store and artifact
# paths, so those variables are only needed for the host-process workflow. See
# services/api/README.md and apps/storefront/README.md.

# --- AI provider (optional) ---
# Without a key the assistant and voice-search surfaces return a typed 503 by
# design; every other capability works.
#
# The defaults below point at OpenRouter, which is the gateway this project is
# developed against, and DeepSeek's cheap model that supports the Responses API.
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys and put it in `OPENAI_API_KEY`; the
# variable name is the OpenAI SDK's, whatever gateway sits behind it.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
SMART_ECOMMERCE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
SMART_ECOMMERCE_ASSISTANT_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash
SMART_ECOMMERCE_TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL=openai/whisper-large-v3

# Using OpenAI directly instead? Clear the base URL — an empty value means the
# default OpenAI endpoint — and set OpenAI model ids:
#   SMART_ECOMMERCE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=
#   SMART_ECOMMERCE_ASSISTANT_MODEL=<model id>
#   SMART_ECOMMERCE_TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL=<model id>
#
# Any other OpenAI-compatible gateway works the same way: set its base URL and
# use its own model ids.

# --- Host-process API (optional) ---
# Point these at the published data-store ports from infra/compose.dev.yaml.
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_POSTGRES_DSN=postgresql://smart_ecommerce:smart_ecommerce@127.0.0.1:55432/smart_ecommerce
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_MONGO_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:57017/?directConnection=true
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_MONGO_DATABASE=smart_ecommerce

# --- Host-process storefront (optional) ---
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_COOKIE_SECURE=1

# --- API tuning (optional) ---
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_MAXIMUM_UPLOAD_BYTES=5242880
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_POSTGRES_POOL_SIZE=48
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_WORKER_THREADS=100
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# SMART_ECOMMERCE_LOG_FORMAT=json
